        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding your patient, an 86-year-old male admitted on 06/01/2000 with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough and reduced exercise tolerance. Chest auscultation revealed widespread expiratory wheeze. Chest X-ray confirmed hyperinflation without consolidation. Arterial blood gas analysis showed mild hypoxaemia. Spirometry was consistent with severe obstructive ventilatory defect. He was treated with nebulised bronchodilators (salbutamol and ipratropium), a course of systemic corticosteroids and supplemental low-flow oxygen. He responded well to treatment with satisfactory improvement in respiratory function. He is discharged home in a stable condition. Please ensure ongoing optimisation of his inhaler therapy and pulmonary rehabilitation referral is considered. Do not hesitate to contact me with any queries.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
